{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785092248,"nonce":"xW5i7dMJuR0sqIUgeVRIjGohmA8=","title":"The workspace feed is implemented twice with a copy-pasted shell command; the debug pod diverges silently","message":"Divergence hazard, low severity today, guaranteed to bite whoever changes the\nfeed. Two independent implementations of \"materialize the inputs, tar them\ninto the pod, make the tree group-writable, release the doorstop\" carry the\n**same shell command string as a literal copy**.\n\nVerified at `bd30a71`. Not part of any ADR-0061 slice.\n\n---\n\n\n1. `drive_workspace` — `crates/scarab-executor-k8s/src/lib.rs:461-473`\n2. `DebugLauncher::launch_debug` — `:1706-1719`\n\nBoth build:\n\n```\ntar -xf - -C {WORKSPACE_MOUNT_PATH} \\\n \u0026\u0026 chmod -R g+rwX {WORKSPACE_MOUNT_PATH} \\\n \u0026\u0026 find {WORKSPACE_MOUNT_PATH} -type d -exec chmod g+s {} ';' \\\n \u0026\u0026 touch {CTL_MOUNT_PATH}/init-done\n```\n\nand both precede it with a `materialize` into a tempdir plus `pack_dir`. The\nconstants are shared; the *semantics* are not — they are two separate string\nliterals that happen to be identical.\n\n\nThe three things this command encodes are all load-bearing and all subtle:\n\n- **`chmod -R g+rwX` + `chmod g+s` on dirs** is the git-bug b04697f fix. The\n  nine-line comment explaining it (`:449-459`) exists **only** at the\n  `drive_workspace` site. A reader at `launch_debug` sees an unexplained\n  `chmod` and has every reason to \"simplify\" it.\n- **`touch {CTL_MOUNT_PATH}/init-done`** is the doorstop release. The waiter\n  is `until [ -f {CTL_MOUNT_PATH}/init-done ]; do sleep 0.2; done` at `:1622`\n  and `:2174` — so the marker name now appears at **four** sites. Change it in\n  three of them and the debug pod hangs forever with no error.\n- The tar's own ownership behaviour (the CAS tarball carries `65532:65532\n  0755` on every entry including `.`, clobbering the mount-time group\n  writability) is the reason the `chmod` is needed at all — also documented\n  only at the first site.\n\nSo a change to the marker or to the chmod semantics silently diverges the\n**debug surface**, which is the surface a human reaches for when something is\nalready wrong. A debug pod that hangs at Init, or whose `/workspace` is\nread-only, is a bad experience at the worst possible moment, and no test\ncovers it (`launch_debug` needs a live cluster).\n\n\nExtract one function that both call — something like\n\n```rust\n/// The feed command: unpack the CAS tarball into /workspace, restore group\n/// writability (b04697f), and release the init doorstop. ONE definition —\n/// `drive_workspace` and `DebugLauncher::launch_debug` must not drift.\nfn workspace_feed_command() -\u003e String\n```\n\nand move the nine-line b04697f comment onto it, so the explanation lives with\nthe code rather than with one of its two callers. Consider also a\n`workspace_wait_command()` for the two doorstop waiters at `:1622`/`:2174`, so\n`init-done` appears once.\n\n\ns3-feed replaces the `drive_workspace` leg with a Scarab-owned fetcher image.\n**It must change `launch_debug` too**, or the debug pod keeps the deleted\ntunnel alive — a `busybox` doorstop and an `exec` tar that survive only in the\ndebug path, unexercised and unowned. Extracting the function first makes that\na one-site change and makes the omission impossible to miss. Doing it as its\nown small commit before s3-feed is cheaper than doing it during.","files":null}]}